  "developmentFailures": [
    "A later fresh-browser run had no visible geometry by 10.055 s and failed the unchanged 10 s budget. The four-large-partition implementation was replaced by up to eight smaller batches, shortest-first, through at most three reusable native workers. A real-engine native diagnostic produced crankcase/pipes by 3.04 s; that diagnostic is not counted as browser acceptance. The final series starts after this scheduling change. Earlier log: .metrics/perf-001/series-before-preview-pool/run-1.log.",
    "The first acceptance series stopped on run 2: viewing passed at 9.843 s and 8.121 s, but run 2 cancellation revealed a stale modeling preview that drew the prior Box twice. Source geometry and camera were unchanged. An initial modeling-preview ownership guard did not resolve it. Tracing the source lists found that a late current exact artifact was appended alongside the existing recipe display source; both drew the same mesh. Current artifact sources now replace display and metadata sources by body ID. Import also clears transient modeling previews. The final five-run series starts after source replacement, with both earlier failure logs retained, including .metrics/perf-001/series-before-source-replacement/run-1.log. Earlier logs are retained in .metrics/perf-001/series-before-preview-ownership-fix/.",
    "Whole-file lightweight preview took about 15.5 s; partitioned native display transfer replaced it.",
    "Initial browser pilot left the scene behind Files; import now opens Solid automatically and the runner requires the canvas to be foreground.",
    "A cancellation camera-restore race was caught and fixed by retaining the saved camera until the restoration frame runs.",
    "Preview/final bounds checks exposed an existing exact-display recentering error for asymmetric parts. Source coordinate alignment and a derived-cache revision fixed it; original STEP and native checkpoint geometry agreed throughout.",
    "The first full verify run timed out clearing the offset-distance field. A profiled focused journey passed; an explicit keyboard-focus assertion was retained and the unprofiled full suite passed. No reproduction or root cause was established for that timeout."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Budget proven for the pinned engine on the declared reference runner; not a promise for every STEP file, device or network.",
